{"slug":"setup-windows","title":"Barkpark on Windows","blocks":[{"id":"b1","type":"ingress","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Two things you can do on Windows, each one command: run a local Barkpark server (Phoenix API + Studio), or install the bp CLI to drive a server / the TUI."}]},{"id":"b2","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Run a local Barkpark server","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (Phoenix API + Studio) — "},{"type":"text","value":"scripts\\setup-windows.ps1","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Install the bp CLI","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" to drive a server / the TUI — a PowerShell one-liner"}]]},{"id":"b3","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Everything below is PowerShell (5.1 or 7+). Tested end-to-end on Windows 11 with Erlang/OTP 28, Elixir 1.20, PostgreSQL 18."}]},{"id":"b4","type":"divider"},{"id":"b5","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"1. Run a local server — one command"},{"id":"b6","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Prerequisites:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" 64-bit Windows 10/11, "},{"type":"text","value":"git","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", and a clone of this repo. That's it — the script installs the rest (no admin, no Visual Studio)."}]},{"id":"b7","type":"code","value":"git clone https://github.com/FRIKKern/barkpark.git\ncd barkpark\n.\\scripts\\setup-windows.ps1"},{"id":"b8","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The script is idempotent and does the whole job:"}]},{"id":"b9","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"installs "},{"type":"text","value":"Scoop","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (user-scoped package manager) if missing"}],[{"type":"text","value":"installs "},{"type":"text","value":"Erlang/OTP + Elixir + PostgreSQL","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" via Scoop"}],[{"type":"text","value":"pins that toolchain ahead of any stale system Erlang/Elixir on your PATH"}],[{"type":"text","value":"initializes + starts a local "},{"type":"text","value":"Postgres","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" cluster (trust auth, "},{"type":"text","value":"postgres","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" superuser)"}],[{"type":"text","value":"fetches deps, "},{"type":"text","value":"compiles","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"text","value":"creates + migrates + seeds","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" the database"}],[{"type":"text","value":"starts "},{"type":"text","value":"Phoenix","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" in its own window and waits until the API answers"}]]},{"id":"b10","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"When it finishes you get:"}]},{"id":"b11","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":""}],[{"type":"text","value":""}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"Studio"}],[{"type":"text","value":"http://localhost:4000/studio","marks":["code"]}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"API"}],[{"type":"text","value":"http://localhost:4000/api/schemas","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (liveness probe — there is no "},{"type":"text","value":"/health","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Reader"}],[{"type":"text","value":"http://localhost:4000/papers/<slug>","marks":["code"]}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Token"}],[{"type":"text","value":"barkpark-dev-token","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (read+write+admin; "},{"type":"text","value":"demo","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" profile)"}]]]},{"id":"b12","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Create a paper"},{"id":"b13","type":"code","value":"irm http://localhost:4000/v1/paperflow/papers -Method Post `\n  -Headers @{Authorization='Bearer paperflow-dev-ingest-token'} `\n  -ContentType 'application/json' `\n  -Body '{\"slug\":\"hello\",\"style\":\"article\",\"blocks\":[{\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":1,\"text\":\"Hello from Windows\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"value\":\"Made on a native Windows dev server.\"}]}]}'"},{"id":"b14","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Then open "},{"type":"text","value":"http://localhost:4000/papers/hello","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Note the block shapes: "},{"type":"text","value":"headings carry text","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":", paragraphs carry "},{"type":"text","value":"content","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (inline nodes)."}]},{"id":"b15","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Daily use"},{"id":"b16","type":"code","value":".\\scripts\\setup-windows.ps1 start     # start Postgres + server (after first setup)\n.\\scripts\\setup-windows.ps1 status    # toolchain + Postgres + API health\n.\\scripts\\setup-windows.ps1 stop      # stop Postgres (close the server window to stop Phoenix)"},{"id":"b17","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Always start the server through this script.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" It sets PATH correctly each run, so you never fight the stale system Erlang/Elixir that Windows keeps ahead of Scoop in fresh shells."}]},{"id":"b18","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Flag"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Effect"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"-Profile clean","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"papers + media schemas only, one admin token printed once (default is "},{"type":"text","value":"demo","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"-Port 4001","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"bind a different port (dev now honors "},{"type":"text","value":"PORT","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"-Recreate","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"drop + recreate the DB (DESTRUCTIVE)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"-NoStart","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"set up everything but don't launch the server"}]]]},{"id":"b19","type":"divider"},{"id":"b20","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"2. Install the bp CLI"},{"id":"b21","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"For connecting to a server, the TUI, and the setup wizard:"}]},{"id":"b22","type":"code","value":"irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FRIKKern/barkpark/main/scripts/install-cli.ps1 | iex\nbp version"},{"id":"b23","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Auto-detects arch, "},{"type":"text","value":"verifies the sha256","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" against the release "},{"type":"text","value":"checksums.txt","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (hard-fails on mismatch), installs to "},{"type":"text","value":"%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Barkpark\\bin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", and adds it to PATH. Then point it anywhere:"}]},{"id":"b24","type":"code","value":"bp setup --target connect --server https://api.example.com --token $env:BARKPARK_TOKEN\nbp whoami"},{"id":"b25","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Env var"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Effect"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_BIN_DIR","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"install dir (default "},{"type":"text","value":"%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Barkpark\\bin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_CLI_VERSION","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"pin a release, e.g. "},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.1","marks":["code"]}]]]},{"id":"b26","type":"callout","tone":"info","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"text","value":"irm | iex","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" form runs in-process and is "},{"type":"text","value":"not","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" blocked by a Restricted execution policy."}]},{"id":"b27","type":"divider"},{"id":"b28","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Media on Windows (ImageMagick)"},{"id":"b29","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Image renditions normally use "},{"type":"text","value":"vix","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/libvips, which has "},{"type":"text","value":"no Windows prebuilt NIF","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":". So on Windows Barkpark uses an "},{"type":"text","value":"ImageMagick backend","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" instead: "},{"type":"text","value":"mix.exs","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" drops the "},{"type":"text","value":"image","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" dep, and "},{"type":"text","value":"Barkpark.Media.ImageBackend","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" shells out to the "},{"type":"text","value":"magick","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" CLI — a plain executable, no NIF. "},{"type":"text","value":"scripts\\setup-windows.ps1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" installs it ("},{"type":"text","value":"scoop install imagemagick","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"); the backend is selected automatically by OS."}]},{"id":"b30","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"All presets work natively — "},{"type":"text","value":"thumb / preview / hero / og, JPEG and WebP","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":". macOS, Linux, Docker, and CI keep using libvips unchanged (byte-identical output there)."}]},{"id":"b31","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer libvips on Windows anyway? Install libvips + a C toolchain and build with "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_WITH_IMAGE=1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", or use Docker."}]},{"id":"b32","type":"divider"},{"id":"b33","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Docker alternative"},{"id":"b34","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"If you prefer containers (or want media without a C toolchain), use Docker Desktop:"}]},{"id":"b35","type":"code","value":"bp setup --target local --docker --yes"},{"id":"b36","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"This runs Postgres + the API in "},{"type":"text","value":"docker compose","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", fully isolated. Requires Docker Desktop running ("},{"type":"text","value":"docker version","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" must succeed). If the CLI can't reach the engine, your Docker Desktop is likely outdated — update it."}]},{"id":"b37","type":"divider"},{"id":"b38","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Manual setup (without the script)"},{"id":"b39","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The Phoenix-from-clone steps are the same as Linux/macOS once a modern toolchain is present — see SETUP.md. The Windows-specific deltas the script handles for you: install via Scoop ("},{"type":"text","value":"scoop install erlang elixir postgresql","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"), start Postgres with "},{"type":"text","value":"pg_ctl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", prepend the Scoop dirs to PATH, and rely on the auto-dropped "},{"type":"text","value":"image","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" dep. For native-from-clone backend work you can also use "},{"type":"text","value":"WSL2","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" and follow "},{"type":"text","value":"SETUP.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" inside Ubuntu."}]},{"id":"b40","type":"divider"},{"id":"b41","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Troubleshooting (Windows)"},{"id":"b42","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"bp","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" not recognized","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — open a new terminal (PATH applies to "},{"type":"text","value":"new","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" sessions), or run "},{"type":"text","value":"& \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\Barkpark\\bin\\bp.exe\" version","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"mix","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"erl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" resolve to an old version","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — a stale system Erlang/Elixir is ahead of Scoop on PATH. The setup script side-steps this by always prepending the Scoop toolchain; use it to run the server. To fix permanently, uninstall the old Erlang/Elixir or move the Scoop dirs earlier in PATH."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Port 4000 in use","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"text","value":"setup-windows.ps1 start -Port 4001","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Postgres won't start","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — check "},{"type":"text","value":"~\\scoop\\apps\\postgresql\\current\\pg.log","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"text","value":"setup-windows.ps1 status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" shows whether it's up."}],[{"type":"text","value":"curl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" does the wrong thing","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — in PowerShell "},{"type":"text","value":"curl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" aliases "},{"type":"text","value":"Invoke-WebRequest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; use "},{"type":"text","value":"irm","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"text","value":"curl.exe","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"SmartScreen flags "},{"type":"text","value":"bp.exe","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — unsigned single binary; the installer's sha256 check is the integrity guarantee. Allow it or pin "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_CLI_VERSION","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]]},{"id":"b43","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Canon: "},{"type":"text","value":"QUICKSTART.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (cross-platform) · "},{"type":"text","value":"SETUP.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (from-source) · "},{"type":"text","value":"../cards/cli.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"bp","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" semantics)."}]}],"related":["setup-setup","setup-quickstart","cards-cli"]}
